  "created": "2026-11-19",
  "validation": {
    "python_tests": "14 passed; POC CLI baseline and bytecode prevention passed",
    "docker_runtime": "macOS scoped read returned 7 containers, 8 distinct images, 2 volumes and 0 duplicate groups. The new Compose projection preserved the legacy request and passed four selected tests. Earlier real Compose lifecycle fixtures are recorded separately.",
    "rust_compiler": "macOS ARM64 Rust 117 tests plus registered integration passed. Earlier Linux ARM64 and Windows ARM64 native evidence belongs to their prior candidates.",
    "html_parse": "passed",
    "agent_integration": "Current macOS Claude 2.1.331, Codex 0.172.0 and Gemini 0.67.0 passed nine actual CLI cases with synthetic replies and a tool stub. On hook error Claude blocked the stub; Codex and Gemini ran it. Read-only MCP regression passed. Earlier native Ubuntu Parallels also passed nine actual CLI cases.",
    "dockerd_broker": "Current macOS a44f0ca passed live same-UID relay and loopback boundary, broker info and temporary GUI launchd restart. Earlier Linux QEMU and Windows ARM64 SCM evidence remains platform-specific.",
    "dashboard": "Current a44f0ca installed macOS API and WebKit at 1060/390 px matched scoped Docker inventory (7 containers, 8 distinct images, 2 volumes, 0 duplicate groups).",
    "release_packages": "Current macOS a44f0ca 0.1.1-rc.1 matched two independent builds, install, upgrade, rollback, re-upgrade and removal. Previous ada5a09 qualification remains for Linux and Windows.",
    "windows_qualification": "Current Windows ARM64 and x64 artifacts had matching repeat packages and passed host PE and package checks. Existing Windows ARM64 NTFS passed the actual same-version ARM64 upgrade, dashboard and removal. x64 binaries and dashboard ran emulated, with install and upgrade rejected and ARM64 installation preserved.",
    "release_signature": "macOS ARM64 offline signer handoff, exact archive and manifest verification, rejected responses, publisher-gated local package rejection, and package lifecycle passed. Official signer qualification remains separate.",
    "build_providers": "Current macOS: six registered tasks in isolated Cargo, Node, pnpm, Gradle, uv and Go projects, plus failure audit, passed. Earlier actual Next.js build and loopback, Playwright traces and TTL passed under their separate fixtures.",
    "documentation_traceability": "Rust tree a44f0ca. WBS 14, DSG stages 8 and requirements 13 matched to artifact and scoped evidence. Fresh Python 14 and Rust 117 plus macOS integration and current package lifecycle passed.",
    "windows_foundation": "Windows ARM64 MSVC cross-link and nine native NTFS filesystem tests passed on the existing Parallels guest. macOS Python 14 and Rust 98 plus registered integration passed.",
    "buildx_cache": "Live isolated default Buildx: 208 records, 208 reclaimable, 8 shared and 167 mutable, with all preserved and no candidates. Read-only BuildKit parser was tested; standalone guest evidence is from the older source.",
    "next_and_compose_health": "macOS Rust 102 and integration passed with the real Next.js 16.4.6 pnpm build, loopback runtime and leases, plus real same-container Compose health rejection and bounded cleanup.",
    "gc_crash_recovery": "macOS Rust 103 and integration passed. Committed GC intent and staged artifact survived an owned child SIGKILL, restored identical identity/SHA-256 with zero deletion and retained exact audit events.",
    "current_macos_qualification": "Rust tree a44f0ca and exact archive hash 67c1fb2045dba5709c4e1b4858c5cb9c922732fedc53b5f3f32cccd50f29c7f4. Two independent builds matched and native package lifecycle, user fixture preservation and installed WebKit/API passed.",
    "compose_live_changes": "The fixture reran Compose and kept one ID. The read-only reuse check matched supplied expectations against the real container and rejected configuration, health, image and tmpfs changes. Matching tmpfs was unknown. Real named volume replacement is recorded separately.",
    "linux_arm64_qualification": "Current ada5a09 static musl on existing Ubuntu ARM64 Parallels passed a previous-package upgrade, managed success, timeout 124 and lease reacquisition, dashboard and removal. Earlier 681be1e also passed the isolated Linux container and Ubuntu Parallels.",
    "standalone_buildkit": "Linux ARM64 on existing Ubuntu Parallels: product and official BuildKit v0.35.1 matched counts 0 and 4. Wrong PID, wrong client digest and socket symlink were rejected; all cache preserved.",
    "named_volume_reuse": "Real isolated Compose reused identical named volume A and one ID. Replacing A with B rejected the old name and accepted the expected new mount. Read-only, nocopy and both volumes preserved verified.",
    "windows_installer_process_architecture": "Current ada5a09 package: on the existing ARM64 Windows Parallels guest, native ARM64 and emulated x64 portable CPython 3.13.9 each returned exit 1 with the expected host mismatch for x64 install and upgrade. Prefix, existing pointer, installed hashes and fixture user file were preserved. Guest was restored to suspended. Current existing Mac/Parallels scope is complete. Windows x64 OS lifecycle is excluded because the registered Windows guest is ARM64.",
    "docker_controlled_gc": "Seven controlled-backend tests passed plus 17 registry and four image regressions. Exact binding, one-use approval, slot exclusion, durable intent and receipt recovery passed. Existing Docker contexts preserve unverified control.",
    "macos_lease_scope": "Runner, registry and process identity tests passed. Owned detached processes retained expired leases during normal exit and forced supervisor termination; when they exited, lease reacquisition and audit passed in throwaway state.",
    "docker_pending_target": "macOS: eight controlled Docker GC tests, 17 registry tests and four image tests passed. An unresolved intent blocks new plans, approvals and old tokens for the same endpoint/kind/ID until receipt recovery settles it. Full Python 14 and Rust 118 plus scoped inventory and Buildx passed. Live dedicated-engine application and recovery remain unverified.",
    "dedicated_docker_preapproval": "Existing Ubuntu ARM64 verified read-only prerequisites, then a transient Docker 29.1.3 engine verified a private Unix peer, isolated mount and network, no TCP listener and denied unprivileged clients. Initial inventory was empty. Exactly one untagged no-layer synthetic image matched the expected configuration digest and deterministic archive digest. Delete requests: zero. Guest suspended; the next test used separate approval for this generation and image.",
    "dedicated_docker_live": "The pinned Ubuntu ARM64 engine and approved image were revalidated. One live no-force/no-parent-prune deletion removed the one disposable image (inventory 1 to 0). The reopened Rust registry settled the persisted receipt after a test-induced interruption. One intent, one applied audit, zero open leases; reuse was rejected. The isolated runtime and scratch directory were reclaimed and the guest was suspended. Default Python 14 and Rust 118 passed with the live test ignored by default. The exact live test passed once when explicitly selected.",
    "buildkit_operating_service": "Ubuntu Parallels ARM64 systemd operated one dedicated socket with two system roles. A single synthetic record was applied and the read-only receipt recovery did not call mutation. Same-generation ledger/checkpoint rollback and a diverging external witness were preserved without backend changes. Guest ext4 receipt and macOS-side independent pin were verified after service cleanup, with four availability cases. Physical host power loss and production project rollout remain separate.",
    "buildkit_project_enrollment": "A pinned Ubuntu ARM64 BuildKit dedicated worker accepted tracked DSG README bytes. The project revision, source SHA-256, LLB, OCI export, native worker and record IDs were bound and four native DB digests were unchanged by read-only qualification. A separate QEMU full VM snapshot restored coherent synthetic RAM and ext4 markers. The off-VM latest marker differed. Production rollout, application-level full-snapshot rejection and physical power interruption are still unverified.",
    "buildkit_external_freshness": "Independent issuance verified a stopped Ubuntu ARM64 worker with five native DBs unchanged. Public apply was preserved when external freshness was absent or denied. The actual Go freshness client used a protected relay to a host authority outside a QEMU full snapshot. One synthetic external claim was recorded and a request after the pre-request restore was denied. Native mutation calls were zero. Production rollout, restoration after the success reply, and a physical power cut remain separate.",
    "buildkit_external_execution": "The external executor reserved one isolated append effect and returned the same settled receipt after bare QEMU full restores at approval and receipt boundaries. The isolated approval store was restored to its earlier state while the independent execution journal and claim remained intact. Ubuntu ARM64 verified the actual CLI with a pinned synthetic child, stale execution state and exact replay. Actual operating deployment, physical power cuts and joint rollback of execution state and claim remained separate in that run.",
    "buildkit_independent_execution_fence": "The Ubuntu ARM64 external executor CLI required an independent one-time reservation outside the guest before a digest-pinned synthetic effect. The saved execution ledger and local marker were jointly rolled back. macOS admitted one reservation, rejected the repeat, and one effect occurred. After restoring the settled files, the same receipt returned without the socket. Production worker mutation, physical power loss, and rollback of the independent reservation were outside this qualification.",
    "local_reclaim_measurement": "The installed macOS ARM64 CLI reclaimed one generated 16,777,216-byte Cargo artifact; expected size and independently observed pre-cleanup file allocation agreed. The protected witness was preserved. The host volume delta is observational. Ubuntu Parallels independently measured 8,192 expected payload allocation bytes for a new exact BuildKit fixture before separate approval, with zero mutations.",
    "local_reclaim_witness": "The initial local BuildKit fixture was rejected before apply because its ledger witness was on tmpfs; the exact target stayed read-only and no apply was dispatched. A replacement local Ubuntu ext4 candidate uses a distinct disk-backed witness and has 8,192 expected payload allocation bytes. The replacement requires its own approval.",
    "buildkit_measured_reclaim": "A separately approved exact BuildKit cache was applied once on disk-file-backed ext4 in Ubuntu Parallels. Estimated and independently observed target allocations matched at 8,192 bytes. The guest filesystem allocation rose from 389,120 to 417,792 bytes, yielding -28,672 bytes net reclaimed. Non-target files and the reopened receipt matched, and the fixture was cleaned. The Mac volume delta is observational.",
    "local_recovery_and_current_arm64_packages": "On Rust tree 13fdb79, current Mac and Parallels Ubuntu and Windows ARM64 packages passed native upgrade, diagnosis, both binaries, read-only dashboard and removal. Live local Docker plan and recheck preserved an existing image without writes; a verified synthetic candidate stayed non-applicable and five exclusive dispatch fixture tests passed. That BuildKit trial recorded an additional 36,864 bytes before the later path-level attribution documented in TASK.md.",
    "local_installation_qualification_5685b45": "Ubuntu ARM64 passed installation, upgrade, diagnosis, read-only dashboard, isolated Moby plans, and uninstall. Both pending deletion subjects and package/engine hashes were rechecked. Actual image application awaits target approval. The byte-identical macOS host and macOS Parallels installations passed both detached process protections, four Chromium click traces, four released leases, and expiration of one success trace. The initial host trial's final exit-proof condition remains undetermined.",
    "macos_exit_diagnostics_and_hook_boundary": "126 Rust tests and the macOS integration suite passed. The candidate installation produced four Chromium click traces, four released leases, no held lease, and one expired success trace removed. Detached process protection and durable exit diagnostics passed. The nine native Claude, Codex and Gemini cases yielded zero writes to the protected synthetic upstream."
  },
